  abstract: |
    This is the registered text of a theory-level registration: twenty-two predictions about systems that improve themselves, and in particular about whether the correction that holds such a system to its specification can keep pace as its capability rises. Each prediction is stated with the circumstances it is claimed to hold under, the observation that would show it false, what falls with it if it fails, whether any instrument exists today that could decide it, and the author’s confidence or his refusal to give one. The wording was fixed on a public registry before any outcome was examined against it. Nothing here is a result.

    This is a registration record and is not a paper; it is not counted in the paper series.

